{"id": "EUVD-2026-71943", "enisaUuid": "629b28ed-ff78-3267-8079-0edb58f932ee", "description": "BookWyrm through 0.9.1 fails to validate user visibility permissions in the status edit endpoint, allowing authenticated attackers to read followers-only and direct-message reviews by enumerating sequential status IDs. Attackers can access the raw content of restricted statuses through the edit view, bypassing the privacy protections documented for these message types.", "datePublished": "2026-09-05T09:59:03", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-24T14:20:58", "baseScore": 7.1, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:H/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/geo-chen/oss/blob/main/bookwyrm.md#finding-1-authenticated-idor-in-editstatus-exposes-private-review-comment-and-quotation-content", "https://github.com/bookwyrm-social/bookwyrm/blob/v0.9.1/bookwyrm/views/status.py", "https://github.com/bookwyrm-social/bookwyrm/blob/v0.9.1/bookwyrm/templates/snippets/create_status/content_field.html", "https://github.com/bookwyrm-social/bookwyrm", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/bookwyrm-through-0.9.1-insecure-direct-object-reference-in-editstatus-exposes-followers-only-and-direct-statuses"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-86111", "GHSA-phg3-p22v-rp9q"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.44, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "918ddae5-a432-34f1-b4c7-3e176495075f", "product": {"name": "bookwyrm", "vendor": {"name": "bookwyrm-social"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22640.9.1"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "381df1ad-fccb-3128-b031-ad03bbf5d00c", "vendor": {"name": "bookwyrm-social"}}], "isExploited": false}